  "body": "A refused post's reason now stays on screen in a \"Post refused\" window. A viewport click no longer erases it.\n\n### What was wrong\n\n- `State::post_program_path` put a refusal only on the status line (\"post refused: <reason>\").\n- The status line is shared. The next viewport click (`interact::pick_model` writes \"selected <name>\" or \"no model under the cursor\"), face or edge pick, or command wrote over it, so the reason was gone before the user could act on it. Posting the seeded demo (refused for a shank hit) and clicking the viewport centre replaces the refusal on the status line with the pick's own line, and on `main` 8f30bee was the only place the reason was shown.\n\n### What changed\n\n- A refused post also keeps its reason in `State::post_refusal` (`PostRefusal { path, reason, doc_version }`). The status line is unchanged.\n- New `egui_app/post_refusal.rs`: a \"Post refused\" window (an in-app `egui::Window`, like the G-code viewer) shows the reason in the error ink, and says nothing was written to the file and a program already there is unchanged. It closes by its ✖, like the G-code viewer. A long reason scrolls.\n- The window goes when the user closes it, when a later post succeeds, or when the document is switched (New, Open).\n- An edit or regenerate after the refusal keeps the window and adds \"The document has changed since this post was refused - post again to check it.\", so the reason is never shown as current when it may not be. A pick does not count as an edit.\n- The window draws nothing while no refusal stands, so no shell snapshot moves.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/265-sticky-post-refusal.md` (sticky status line, closing on any edit, and putting the refusal in the G-code viewer were considered and dropped). PR #232's status-strip alert styling is separate and doesn't conflict: it makes a refusal stand out while it is on the line, and this keeps it after the line moves on.\n\n### Tests (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/post_refusal.rs`, through the real shell layout)\n\n- `a_refused_posts_reason_survives_a_viewport_click`: post the seed (refused), click the viewport centre. The status line moves on, and the window still shows the gate's exact reason. No changed-since note, and no file written.\n- `an_edit_after_the_refusal_notes_it_and_a_successful_post_retires_it`: the skim edit and regenerate keep the reason and add the note; the skim then posts and the window is gone.\n- `closing_the_refusal_window_retires_it` and `a_new_document_retires_the_refusal`.\n- With the window call taken back out of `shell.rs` (`git stash` of that file only), `a_refused_posts_reason_survives_a_viewport_click` fails (\"a refused post opens its window\"). The other three read the new `State::post_refusal` field, so they don't build without the fix.\n\n### What ran (Windows 10, local, built from upstream `main` 8f30bee plus this commit)\n\n- The quick gate's plan for this diff (`scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -DryRun`, run by hand with `-j 3` because another session was using most of the CPU): ui lib plus `boundary`, `boundary_picks`, `feedback`, `fixtures`, `gpu_render`, `machine`, `models`, `operations`, `shell`, `theme_files`. 367 pass, 2 ignored, 3 fail (below).\n- The only failures are the three UI pixel snapshots (`egui_shell_snapshot`, `egui_shell_snapshot_light`, `tool_editor_snapshot`). They fail on clean `main` on this machine by the same pixel counts (1544, 1815, 2080; #255). The new window draws nothing without a refusal, so it doesn't touch them.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Not run: the windowed app by hand (the tests drive the real `shell_layout` through egui_kittest, including the viewport click), Linux, macOS.\n- `state.rs` is already far past the 400-line law; this adds one field, its init and four lines in the post and document-switch paths. The window and its type live in the new `egui_app/post_refusal.rs` (78 lines), and the tests in a child module of `tests.rs` so they reuse its shell harness.\n\nChangelog: A refused post's reason stays on screen in a \"Post refused\" window until you close it, post successfully, or switch documents, instead of vanishing at the next click (#265)\n\nFixes #265\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
